        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/18/wrap-up-for-wednesday-november-18-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><b><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Roll Call
Votes<u></u></span></b></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Motion to waive budget points of order with respect to Cal.
     #453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act; agreed to:
     70-26.</span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
     &quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Adoption of </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;">Capito substitute amendment
     #6883; adopted: 69-27.</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;
     color:windowtext">Motion to invoke cloture on Cal. #453 H.R.2347
     Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act, as amended; agreed to:
     65-31.</span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
     &quot;Times New Roman&quot;"></span></li>
</ol><p><b><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></b></p><p><b><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Legislative
Business</span></b></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Passed the
following bills:</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">H.R.2478 –
Financial Exploitation Prevention Act</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">S.4445 – Veterans
Protection from Fraud Act of 2026</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Notwithstanding
Rule 22, at a time to be determined by the Majority Leader, in concurrence with
the Democratic Leader, no later than Friday, November 20th, H.Con.Res.93 will
be discharged from the Committee on Foreign Relations and the Senate will
proceed to its consideration. There will be 6 hours for debate only, with the
time equally divided between the Leaders or their designees on the concurrent
resolution. Following the use or yielding back of that time, the Senate will
vote on the concurrent resolution.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p>



















</p><p><b><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">No
Additional Executive Business</span></b></p>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
