      <item>
        <title>Schedule for Tuesday, November 17, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/16/schedule-for-tuesday-november-17-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:25:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Senate Schedule]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/16/schedule-for-tuesday-november-17-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">The Senate
stands adjourned until 10:00am on Tuesday, November 17, 2026.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Following
Leader remarks, the Senate will resume consideration of Capito substitute
amendment #6883, post-cloture.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">The Senate
will recess from 12:30pm until 2:15pm to allow for the weekly caucus meetings.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">At 2:15pm the
Senate will proceed to Executive Session and vote on the confirmation of
Executive Calendar #944 Anna St. John, of Louisiana, to be United States
Circuit Judge for the Fifth Circuit. 
Upon disposition of the St. John nomination, the Senate will resume
Legislative Session.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Additional
votes are possible during Tuesday’s session. 
Senators will be notified when more information is available.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><u><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Tuesday,
November 17<sup>th</sup> at approx. 2:15pm – 1 roll call vote:</span></u><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"></span></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
<li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Confirmation Executive Calendar
#944 Anna St. John, of Louisiana, to be United States Circuit Judge for
the Fifth Circuit</span></li>
</ol><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">As
a reminder, cloture has been filed on the following:</span></p><p>
</p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
<li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Cal.
#453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act</span></li>
<li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Executive
Calendar #968 Richard Wesley Bennett, of Texas, to be United States
District Judge for the Southern District of Texas</span></li>
<li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Executive
Calendar #969 Courtney Leigh Coker, of Texas, to be United States District
Judge for the Northern District of Texas</span></li>
<li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Executive
Calendar #970 Kyle Frederick Reardon, of Alaska, to be United States
District Judge for the District of Alaska</span></li>
<li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Executive
Calendar #967 Daniel Lewis Ballou, of Kentucky, to be United States
District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky</span></li>
</ol>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Schedule for Monday, November 16, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/12/schedule-for-monday-november-16-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:05:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Senate Schedule]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/12/schedule-for-monday-november-16-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><font face="Arial">The Senate
stands adjourned until 3:00pm on Monday, November 16, 2026.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Following
Leader remarks, the Senate will proceed to Executive Session and resume
consideration of Executive Calendar #901
Daniel Desmond Domenico, of Colorado, to be United States Circuit Judge for the
Tenth Circuit.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">At
approximately 5:30pm, the Senate will vote on confirmation
of the Domenico nomination.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Following
disposition of the nomination, the Senate will vote on the motion to invoke
cloture on Capito substitute amendment #6883.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><u><font face="Arial">Monday,
November 16<sup>th</sup> at approx. 5:30pm – 2 roll call votes expected:</font></u></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Confirmation of Executive Calendar #901
     Daniel Desmond Domenico, of Colorado, to be United States Circuit Judge
     for the Tenth Circuit.</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to invoke cloture on Capito substitute amendment #6883</font></li>
</ol><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">As
a reminder, cloture has been filed on the following:</font></p><p>

























</p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Capito
     substitute amendment #6883 to Cal. #453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American
     Affordability and Jobs Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Cal.
     #453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><font face="Arial">Executive
     Calendar #968 Richard Wesley Bennett, of Texas, to be United States
     District Judge for the Southern District of Texas</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><font face="Arial">Executive
     Calendar #969 Courtney Leigh Coker, of Texas, to be United States District
     Judge for the Northern District of Texas</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><font face="Arial">Executive
     Calendar #970 Kyle Frederick Reardon, of Alaska, to be United States
     District Judge for the District of Alaska</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><font face="Arial">Executive
     Calendar #967 Daniel Lewis Ballou, of Kentucky, to be United States
     District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky</font></li>
</ol>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Wrap Up for Thursday, November 12, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/12/wrap-up-for-thursday-november-12-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:04:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Wrap Up]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/12/wrap-up-for-thursday-november-12-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><b><font face="Arial">Roll Call
Votes</font></b></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #945 Gregory Carl Cook, of
     Alabama, to be United States District Judge for the Northern District of
     Alabama; invoked: 50-27.</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Confirmation
     of Executive Calendar #945 Gregory Carl Cook, of Alabama, to be United
     States District Judge for the Northern District of Alabama; confirmed:
     49-27.</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #901
     Daniel Desmond Domenico, of Colorado, to be United States Circuit Judge
     for the Tenth Circuit; invoked: 51-27.</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #944
     Anna St. John, of Louisiana, to be United States Circuit Judge for the
     Fifth Circuit; invoked: 49-26.</font></li>
</ol><p><b><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></b></p><p><b><font face="Arial">Legislative
Business</font></b></p><p><font face="Arial">Passed the
following bills:</font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.1353 - to
extend the authority for modifications to the Second Division Memorial in the
District of Columbia </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.3493 -
Carson City Public Land Correction Act </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.2887 –
Route 66 National Historic Trail Designation Act </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.432 – Fort
Ontario Holocaust Refugee Shelter National Historical Park Establishment Act </font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Adopted
S.Res.834 – Golf Course Superintendents Association of America 100th
Anniversary</font></p><p><u><span style="text-decoration:none"><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></span></u></p><p><u><font face="Arial">Amendments
pending to Cal. #453, H.R.2347, BAAJA:</font></u></p><ul style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     for Capito substitute <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6883">#6883</a></font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6884">#6884</a> to #6883</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6885">#6885</a> to #6884</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6886">#6886</a> to the
     underlying bill</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6887">#6887</a> to #6886</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     motion to commit to Finance with amendment <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6888">#6888</a></font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6889">#6889</a> to #6888</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6890">#6890</a> to #6889</font></li>
</ul><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Notwithstanding
Rule 22, at a time to be determined by the Majority Leader, in concurrence with
the Democratic Leader, no later than Friday, November 20th, H.Con.Res.93 will
be discharged from the Committee on Foreign Relations and the Senate will
proceed to its consideration. There will be 6 hours for debate only, with the
time equally divided between the Leaders or their designees on the concurrent
resolution. Following the use or yielding back of that time, the Senate will
vote on the concurrent resolution.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><b><font face="Arial">Executive
Business</font></b></p><p><font face="Arial">Confirmed the
following nomination:</font></p><p><font face="Arial">NAVY</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Executive
Calendar #893 – Rear Adm. Mark D. Behning to be Vice Admiral</font></p><p><b><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></b></p><p>













































</p><p><font face="Arial">At
a time to be determined by the Majority Leader in consultation with the
Democratic Leader, the Senate will on confirmation of Executive Calendar #944 Anna St. John, of Louisiana, to
be United States Circuit Judge for the Fifth Circuit.</font></p>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Schedule for Thursday, November 12, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/11/schedule-for-thursday-november-12-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:05:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Senate Schedule]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/11/schedule-for-thursday-november-12-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The Senate
stands adjourned until 12:00pm on Thursday, November 12, 2026.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Following
Leader remarks, the Senate will proceed to Executive Session to resume
consideration of Executive Calendar #945 Gregory Carl Cook, of Alabama, to be
United States District Judge for the Northern District of Alabama.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">At
approximately 1:00pm the Senate will vote on the motion to invoke cloture on
the Cook nomination.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Additional
votes are expected during Thursday’s session, Senators will be notified when
more information is available.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">During
Wednesday’s session Senator Thune filed cloture on the Thune-Capito substitute
amendment #6883 and the underlying bill Cal. #453, H.R.2347 the legislative
vehicle for the Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act. The first
degree filing deadline for amendments to the substitute and the underlying bill
is 1:00pm Thursday, November 12.&nbsp; The
filing deadline for second degree amendments is 1 hour prior to the cloture
vote, if cloture is invoked.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><u><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Thursday,
November 12, at approx. 1:00pm, roll call vote:</span></u></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Motion to invoke cloture on
     Executive Calendar #945 Gregory Carl Cook, of Alabama, to be United States
     District Judge for the Northern District of Alabama</span></li>
</ol><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><u><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Amendments
pending to Cal. #453, H.R.2347, BAAJA:</span></u></p><ul style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     for Capito Substitute <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6883">#6883</a></span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6884">#6884</a></span> to #6883</li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6885">#6885</a></span> to #6884</li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6886">#6886</a></span> to the
     underlying bill</li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6887">#6887</a></span> to #6886</li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     motion to commit to finance with amendment <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6888">#6888</a></span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6889">#6889</a></span> to #6888</li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     <a href="https://ats.senate.gov/Display.aspx?ID=6890">#6890</a></span> to #6889</li>
</ul><p><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Cloture
has been filed on the following:</span></p><p>

































</p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Executive Calendar </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;">#945 Gregory Carl Cook, of
     Alabama, to be United States District Judge for the Northern District of
     Alabama</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Executive Calendar </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;">#901 Daniel Desmond Domenico,
     of Colorado, to be United States Circuit Judge for the Tenth Circuit</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">Executive Calendar </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;">#944 Anna St. John, of
     Louisiana, to be United States Circuit Judge for the Fifth Circuit</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Thune
     for Capito Substitute #6883 to Cal. #453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American
     Affordability and Jobs Act</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Cal.
     #453 H.R.2347 Bipartisan American Affordability and Jobs Act</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Executive
     Calendar #968 Richard Wesley Bennett, of Texas, to be United States
     District Judge for the Southern District of Texas</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Executive
     Calendar #969 Courtney Leigh Coker, of Texas, to be United States District
     Judge for the Northern District of Texas</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Executive
     Calendar #970 Kyle Frederick Reardon, of Alaska, to be United States
     District Judge for the District of Alaska</span></li>
 <li style="margin-left: 0in;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;">Executive
     Calendar #967 Daniel Lewis Ballou, of Kentucky, to be United States
     District Judge for the Eastern District of Kentucky</span></li>
</ol>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
