      <item>
        <title>Wrap Up for Tuesday, November 10, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/10/wrap-up-for-tuesday-november-10-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:20:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Wrap Up]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/10/wrap-up-for-tuesday-november-10-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><b><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Roll Call
Vote<u></u></span></b></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
<li style="margin-left:0in;"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;">Motion
to proceed to Cal. #453, H.R.2347, legislative vehicle for the Bipartisan
American Affordability and Jobs Act; agreed to 62-21.</span></li>
</ol><p><b><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></b></p><p><b><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Legislative
Business</span></b></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Passed the
following bills:</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Cal. #666,
S.3720 – Bay Area Trail Study</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Cal. #685,
S.3923 – Weather Research and Forecasting Innovation Reauthorization Act of
2026 w/ Cruz-Cantwell substitute amendment</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">S.2434 –
Dayton Aviation Heritage</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">H.R.4930 – To
expand the sharing of information with respect to suspected violations of
intellectual property rights in trade</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Adopted the
following resolutions:</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">S.Res.472 –
International Day of Political Prisoners</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">S.Res.951 –
National Infant Mortality Awareness Month</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">S.Res.950 –
National Clean Energy Week</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">S.Res.955 -
Toys for Tots</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Notwithstanding
Rule 22, at a time to be determined by the Majority Leader, in concurrence with
the Democratic Leader, no later than Friday, November 20th, H.Con.Res.93 will
be discharged from the Committee on Foreign Relations and the Senate will
proceed to its consideration. There will be 6 hours for debate only, with the
time equally divided between the Leaders or their designees on the concurrent
resolution. Following the use or yielding back of that time, the Senate will
vote on the concurrent resolution.</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p><b><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Executive
Business</span></b></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Confirmed the
following nominations:</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">ARMY</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#923 – Brig. Gen. David C. Phillips to be Lieutenant General </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#924 – Lt. Gen. Kevin D. Admiral to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">AIR FORCE</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#925 – Maj. Gen. Charles S. Corcoran (Retired) to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">ARMY</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#926 – Col. Michael L. Seek to be Brigadier General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#927 – Lt. Gen. Edmond M. Brown to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#928 – Lt. Gen. Francisco J. Lozano to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#929 – Maj. Gen. Christopher R. Norrie to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">NAVY</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#930 – Rear Adm. (lh) John D. Saccomando to be Rear Admiral</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">SPACE FORCE</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#931 – Maj. Gen. Robert J. Hutt to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#932 – Maj. Gen. Christopher S. Povak to be Lieutenant General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">NAVY</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#933 – Rear Adm. Oliver T. Lewis to be Vice Admiral</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">AIR FORCE</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#934 – Col. Nathan T. Colunga to be Brigadier General </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#935 – Brig. Gen. Andrew J. Camacho to be Major General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">NAVY </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#936 – Capt. Douglas Graber to be Rear Admiral (lower half)</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">ARMY</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#938 – Col. Kevin H. Miller to be Brigadier General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#939 – Brig. Gen. Paul T. Sellars to be Major General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#940 – Col. Shawn D. Wray to be Brigadier General </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#941 – Col. Ryan T. Smith to be Brigadier General</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#942 – Col. Michael F. Belenky to be Brigadier General </span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Exec. Cal.
#943 – the following to be Brigadier General:</span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Matthew T. Adamczyk    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Robert S. Adcock    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
James E. Armstrong, III    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Jessie J. Brewster    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Sean P. Coakley    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Elizabeth H. Curtis    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Christopher M. Dempsey    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
John B. Gilliam    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Charles A. Green    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Tyson J. Hise    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Timothy P. Hudson    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Justin D. Hufnagel    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Robin D. Husted    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Cullen A. Jones    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Ricardo D. Jones    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Charles W. Kean    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Neal J. Lape    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Ian J. Lauer    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Christopher S. McClure    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Patrick R. Nelson    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Jeffrey W. Pickler    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Joshua R. Ruisanchez    </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Gerald P. Schuck</span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Robert M. Shaw  </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Christopher M. Stauder  </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Ricardo A. Turner  </span></p><p style="margin-left:.5in"><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">Col.
Graham R. White</span></p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif"> </span></p><p>
</p><p><span style="font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif">And all
nominations on the Secretary’s Desk in the Air Force with the exception of
PN970-2, PN1263 Chance J. Pritchard, PN1264 Bryan W. Case, PN1266-1 Jacob P.
Batt and Chelsea L. Waggoner; Army with the exception of PN1017-2 Michael D.
Thompson, PN1061-2, PN1065-2, PN1072-2, PN1189-1 Parker J. Schnetz, PN1224,
PN1308 Roseann P. Apuron; Marine Corps; Navy with the exception of PN835-2 and
PN925; and Space force with the exception of PN1349 Douglas B. Ruyle</span></p>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Schedule for Tuesday, November 10, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/09/schedule-for-tuesday-november-10-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:03:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Senate Schedule]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/11/09/schedule-for-tuesday-november-10-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><font face="Arial">The Senate
stands adjourned until 12:00 noon on Tuesday, November 10, 2026.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Following
Leader remarks, the Senate will resume consideration of the motion to proceed
to Cal. #453, H.R.2347, legislative vehicle for the Bipartisan American
Affordability and Jobs Act, post-cloture.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">All time
during adjournment, recess, morning business, and Leader remarks will count
post-cloture on the motion to proceed.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">The Senate
will recess from 12:30pm until 2:15pm to allow for the weekly caucus meetings.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p>

















</p><p><font face="Arial">Roll call
votes are expected during Tuesday’s session.&nbsp;</font></p>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
