      <item>
        <title>Schedule for Wednesday, September 30, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/09/29/schedule-for-wednesday-september-30-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:21:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Senate Schedule]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/09/29/schedule-for-wednesday-september-30-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><span style="font-family: Arial;">The Senate
stands adjourned until 10:15am on Wednesday, September 30, 2026.</span></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Following
Leader remarks, the Senate will be in a period of morning business with
senators permitted to speak therein for up to ten minutes each.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">During
Monday’s session, Senator Thune filed cloture on the following: </font></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to proceed to Cal. #548 H.R.7008, Stop Insider Trading Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to proceed to Cal. #684 H.R.9340, Ratepayer Protection Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Executive
     Calendar #912 Keith Sonderling, of Florida, to be Secretary of Labor</font></li>
</ol><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">At
approximately 11:30am, the Senate will vote on the motion to invoke cloture on
the motion to proceed to Cal. #548 H.R.7008, Stop Insider Trading Act. If
cloture is not invoked, the Senate will vote on the motion to invoke cloture on
the motion to proceed to Cal. #684, H.R.9340 Ratepayer Protection Act. If
cloture is not invoked, the Senate will vote on the motion to invoke cloture on
Executive Calendar #912 Keith Sonderling, of Florida, to be Secretary of Labor.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Additional
roll call votes are possible during Wednesday’s session.</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><u><font face="Arial">Wednesday,
September 30<sup>th</sup> at approx. 11:30am – up to 3 roll call votes:</font></u></p><p>

























</p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to invoke cloture on the motion to proceed to Cal. #548 H.R.7008, Stop
     Insider Trading Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to invoke cloture on the motion to proceed to Cal. #684, H.R.9340,
     Ratepayer Protection Act</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to invoke cloture on Executive Calendar #912 Keith Sonderling, of Florida,
     to be Secretary of Labor</font></li>
</ol>]]>
        </description>
      </item>
      <item>
        <title>Wrap Up for Tuesday, September 29, 2026</title>
        <link>https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/09/29/wrap-up-for-tuesday-september-29-2026</link>
        <pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:20:00 EST</pubDate>
        <dc:creator>
          <![CDATA[The Senate Democratic Caucus]]>
        </dc:creator>
        <category>
          <![CDATA[Wrap Up]]>
        </category>
        <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.democrats.senate.gov/2026/09/29/wrap-up-for-tuesday-september-29-2026</guid>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><b><font face="Arial">Roll Call
Votes</font></b></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to proceed to Cal. #456, S.J.Res.197, disapproving the rule submitted by
     the Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services of the Department of
     Health and Human Services relating to "Patient Protection and
     Affordable Care Act, HHS Notice of Benefit and Payment Parameters for
     2027; and Basic Health Program"; not agreed to: 48-51.</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">Motion
     to discharge S.Res.852, requesting information on Israel's human rights
     practices pursuant to section 502B(c) of the Foreign Assistance Act of
     1961; not agreed to: 47-51.</font></li>
</ol><p><b><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></b></p><p><b><font face="Arial">Legislative
Business</font></b></p><p><font face="Arial">Passed the
following bills:</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Cal. #492,
H.R.1550, to redesignate Saratoga National Historical Park as Saratoga National
Battlefield Park</font></p><p><font face="Arial">H.R.1945,
America’s National Churchill Museum National Historic Landmark</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Cal. #535,
H.R.3620, Southcentral Foundation Land Transfer Act</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Cal. #459,
S.3383, Unlocking Native Lands and Opportunities for Commerce and Key Economic
Developments Act, w/Schatz sub amdt </font></p><p><font face="Arial">Cal. #682,
S.3219, Albuquerque Indian School Act</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Cal. #620,
S.5045, The Wildfire Emissions Prevention Act </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.528 – GLRI
Act w/Peters sub amdt </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.1574 –
Tribal Access to Electronic Evidence Act w/ Cortez Masto sub amdt</font></p><p><font face="Arial">H.R.5284 –
Claiming Age Clarity Act</font></p><p><font face="Arial">H.R.1190 –
Expanding Access to Capital for Rural Job Creators Act</font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.5600 -
Dennis John Benigno Traumatic Brain Injury Program Reauthorization Act
(Armstrong/Kim)</font></p><p><font face="Arial">H.R.1744 – US
Commission on International Religious Freedom Reauthorization</font></p><p><font face="Arial">H.R.10159 -
Fort Bragg</font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Adopted the
following resolutions:</font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.662 –
Honoring Nicholas Douglas Quets </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.917 -
Dystonia Awareness Month </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.922 -
Day of the Deployed </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.923 -
National 4-H Week </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.924 -
Energy Efficiency Day </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.925 -
Spinal Cord Injury Awareness Month </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.926 -
Literacy Month </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.927 -
National Character Counts Week </font></p><p><font face="Arial">S.Res.928 -
Senate Legal Counsel </font></p><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p><font face="Arial">Began the
Rule 14 process to place the following bills on the Legislative Calendar of
Business:</font></p><ol style="margin-top:0in">
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">S.5602,
     to prohibit the use of Federal funds for the planning and construction of
     any structure or monument at Memorial Circle at Columbia Island/ Lady Bird
     Johnson Park in the District of Columbia. (Merkley)</font></li>
 <li style="margin-left:0in;"><font face="Arial">S.5603,<span style="font-size: 11pt;"> </span>to prohibit the demolition of
     Presidential memorials (Merkley)</font></li>
</ol><p><font face="Arial">&nbsp;</font></p><p>



































































</p><p><b><font face="Arial">No
Executive Business</font></b></p>]]>
